{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>Zaphenath-paneach.</b> Notarikon: צדיק פטפט נגד תאותו — פוטיפר ענה נפשו חנם: 'a righteous one who spied out against his desire — Potiphar afflicted his soul for nothing.'" "<b>And he gave him Osnat.</b> And if you ask: Joseph was king — how did he marry the daughter of a commoner? It seems that since at first Joseph was a slave to Potiphar, he said in his heart: If I do not do his will to marry his daughter, he will demean me and inform against me that I was his slave; I will marry her and he will honor me. And further, one may say that he married her because she was of the seed of Jacob, as Rashi explained in וישלח — that she was the daughter of Dinah from Shechem, and Jacob our father hung an amulet around her neck and cast her out, and she was brought to Egypt by a miracle, as I have explained, and Potiphar raised her in his house, and therefore she was called by his name, just as we find with Moses our master, peace be upon him: ״אלה בני בתיה״ etc. And when Joseph passed through all the land of Egypt, all the women went out to see Joseph's beauty, as it is written ״בנות צעדה עלי שור״, and each one threw him an object or an ornament, but this one had nothing to throw, so she threw him the amulet that was around her neck. He examined it and saw that she was of the seed of Jacob, and he married her."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:58.037032133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}